WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Food

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Jobs

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Development

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Shipping

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.500
Tourism 

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.500
New medicines,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.000
innovation and technology

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.500
Clean, renewable energy

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.500
Our ocean offers all this and more.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.000
This blue economy means hope and prosperity, for all.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.000
The world's ocean economy is currently estimated at around 1.3 trillion euros.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.500
By 2030 it is forecast to more than double.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Aquaculture,

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.500
offshore and ocean energy,

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.500
blue biotech,

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.000
and tourism –

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.500
all hold huge untapped capacity,

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.500
especially in developing countries.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:39.000
Training and education will be key to success. 

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.000
We need to equip a new generation with the necessary “blue skills”.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.500
And we need investment in sustainable solutions.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.500
Quick gains must be discarded in favour of long-term goals. 

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.200
To responsibly use our shared resource, for both present and future generations.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.000
To harvest the full potential of the Blue Economy in a smart, sustainable and inclusive way:

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.000
How will we reach across borders,

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.000
sectors

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.000
and disciplines

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.500
to make it reality?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.500
How do we ensure that the blue economy doesn’t just work for us

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.000
but also for Our Ocean?

